@section 4. ZIL (Zork Implementation Language)

@subsection Supported Constructs
All canonical constructs fully supported.

@subsection Excluded Constructs
@strong{<TELL> dialogue nodes:} ZIL's @code{<TELL>} form generates variable assignments + library calls, not canonical @code{:dialogue} nodes. Justification: Dialogue is backend-specific (screen print vs. speaker audio vs. text file); no single AST node is universal. Resolution: @code{<TELL actor "message">} → @code{(:move :from actor :to DialogueActor)} + @code{(:call :target "DialogueRoutine" :library t :using "message")}.

@subsection Proposed Syntax for Missing Constructs
None.

