@section 7. Lua

@subsection Supported Constructs
@code{:+}, @code{:-}, @code{:×}, @code{:÷}, @code{=}, @code{≠}, @code{<}, @code{≤}, @code{>}, @code{≥}, @code{:and}, @code{:or}, @code{¬}, @code{:if}, @code{:perform}, @code{:goto}, @code{:call}, @code{:method}, @code{:move}, @code{:subscript}, @code{:of}, @code{:bit-and}, @code{:bit-or}, @code{:bit-xor}, @code{:bit-not}, @code{(:ash :value @var{v} :shift @var{n})}, @code{:null}, @code{:self}, @code{:goback}

@subsection Excluded Constructs
@strong{Exponentiation:} Lua's @code{^} operator not supported. Justification: No canonical @code{:exponent} node in EIGHTBOL AST; exponentiation rare in embedded systems. Resolution: User must implement @code{POW(x, y)} library function.

@subsection Proposed Syntax for Missing Constructs
@strong{String reference modification:} @code{string.sub(s, start, length)} → @code{(:refmod :base s :start start :length length)}

