@section 8. Pascal

@subsection Supported Constructs
@code{:+}, @code{:-}, @code{:×}, @code{:÷}, @code{=}, @code{≠}, @code{<}, @code{≤}, @code{>}, @code{≥}, @code{:and}, @code{:or}, @code{¬}, @code{:if}, @code{:perform}, @code{:evaluate}, @code{:call}, @code{:move}, @code{:subscript}, @code{:of}, @code{:address-of}, @code{:log-fault}, @code{:debug-break}, @code{:goback}

@subsection Excluded Constructs
@strong{Set type and operations:} Pascal's @code{SET OF} type and set operations (@code{+}, @code{*}, @code{-}, @code{IN}) not supported. Justification: Sets are specialized; rare in 8-bit/16-bit embedded systems. Most game/embedded code uses arrays or bitmaps instead. Resolution: User compiles sets to arrays or bit vectors manually.

@strong{WITH statement:} Pascal's @code{WITH record DO stmts} expands to explicit @code{:of} field accesses in parser. Justification: @code{WITH} is syntactic sugar; no new semantics. Resolution: @code{WITH rec DO x := rec.a} → @code{(:move :from (:of a rec) :to X)}

@subsection Proposed Syntax for Missing Constructs
@strong{String length:} @code{StringLength(s)} function → @code{(:string-length :target s)}

@strong{String copy:} @code{StringCopy(src, dest, length)} function → @code{(:string-blt :source src :dest dest :length length)}

@strong{String find:} @code{StringFind(haystack, needle)} function → @code{(:string-find :haystack haystack :needle needle)}

---

@section 9. Lingo (Macromedia Director)

@subsection Supported Constructs
@code{:+}, @code{:-}, @code{:×}, @code{:÷}, @code{=}, @code{≠}, @code{<}, @code{≤}, @code{>}, @code{≥}, @code{:and}, @code{:or}, @code{¬}, @code{:if}, @code{:perform}, @code{:call}, @code{:invoke}, @code{:move}, @code{:of}, @code{:subscript}, @code{:bit-and}, @code{:bit-or}, @code{:bit-xor}, @code{:bit-not}, @code{:goback}

@subsection Excluded Constructs
@strong{Director engine features:} Lingo's sprites, channels, behaviors, event handlers not supported. Justification: Director is multimedia-specific; EIGHTBOL targets computation on 8-bit/16-bit systems. Resolution: Map game-specific code to variable assignments + library calls (like AGI/SCI).

@subsection Proposed Syntax for Missing Constructs
@strong{Bitwise AND:} @code{a AND-BIT b} → @code{(:bit-and a b)}

@strong{Bitwise OR:} @code{a OR-BIT b} → @code{(:bit-or a b)}

@strong{Bitwise XOR:} @code{a XOR-BIT b} → @code{(:bit-xor a b)}

@strong{Bitwise NOT:} @code{NOT-BIT a} → @code{(:bit-not a)}

@strong{String length:} @code{StringLength(s)} function → @code{(:string-length :target s)}

@strong{String substring:} @code{StringSubstring(s, start, len)} function → @code{(:refmod :base s :start start :length len)}

