@section 10. Smalltalk

@subsection Supported Constructs
@code{:+}, @code{:-}, @code{:×}, @code{:÷}, @code{=}, @code{≠}, @code{<}, @code{≤}, @code{>}, @code{≥}, @code{:and}, @code{:or}, @code{¬}, @code{:if}, @code{:perform}, @code{:invoke}, @code{:move}, @code{:of}, @code{:subscript}, @code{:goback}

@subsection Excluded Constructs
@strong{First-class blocks/closures:} Smalltalk's blocks (@code{[x + 1]}) compile inline to @code{:procedure} nodes, not preserved as first-class closures. Justification: Closures require runtime function pointers; 8-bit systems rarely support. Resolution: Blocks become inline procedure definitions.

@strong{Message cascading:} Smalltalk's @code{obj msg1; msg2; msg3} expands to separate @code{:invoke} statements. Justification: Cascading is syntactic sugar; no new semantics.

@strong{Reflection/late binding:} Smalltalk's polymorphism and runtime method lookup not supported. Justification: Requires runtime type system; impossible on 8-bit systems.

@subsection Proposed Syntax for Missing Constructs
None (all missing features are compile-time expansions or design exclusions).

---

@section 11. FORTRAN

@subsection Supported Constructs
@code{:+}, @code{:-}, @code{:×}, @code{:÷}, @code{=}, @code{≠}, @code{<}, @code{≤}, @code{>}, @code{≥}, @code{:and}, @code{:or}, @code{¬}, @code{:if}, @code{:perform}, @code{:call}, @code{:move}, @code{:subscript}, @code{:goback}

@subsection Excluded Constructs
@strong{Exponentiation (`**`):} Not supported. Justification: No canonical @code{:exponent} node in EIGHTBOL AST. Resolution: User implements @code{POW(x, y)} library function.

@strong{String concatenation (`//`):} Not supported. Justification: FORTRAN on 8-bit systems rarely uses strings; concatenation is low-priority. Resolution: Use fixed-size string buffers; no concatenation operator.

@strong{COMMON blocks:} Not supported. Justification: FORTRAN 77 artifact; modern FORTRAN uses MODULEs. Variables must be declared in copybooks. Resolution: All variables are globals (from copybook) or instance slots (from copybook); no implicit COMMON.

@subsection Proposed Syntax for Missing Constructs
None. All variable declarations generate copybook entries.

