@section 17. Objective-C

@subsection Supported Constructs
@code{:+}, @code{:-}, @code{:×}, @code{:÷}, @code{=}, @code{≠}, @code{<}, @code{≤}, @code{>}, @code{≥}, @code{:and}, @code{:or}, @code{¬}, @code{:if}, @code{:perform}, @code{:call}, @code{:invoke}, @code{:move}, @code{:subscript}, @code{:of}, @code{:address-of}, @code{:goback}

@subsection Excluded Constructs
@strong{Advanced OO features:} Categories, protocols, formal class hierarchies not supported. Justification: Requires runtime class system; impossible on 8-bit targets. Core OO (message sends, method dispatch) via @code{:invoke} nodes.

@strong{Exception handling:} Objective-C's @code{@@try/@catch/@finally} not supported. Justification: Requires runtime exception stack; 8-bit systems use error codes instead.

@subsection Proposed Syntax for Missing Constructs
None. Core C + message sends sufficient.

