@node Summary: Proposed Syntax

@section Summary: New Syntax Proposed

| Language | Construct | Proposed Syntax | Produces |
|----------|-----------|-----------------|----------|
| Pascal | String length | @code{StringLength(s)} | @code{(:string-length :target s)} |
| Pascal | String copy | @code{StringCopy(src, dest, len)} | @code{(:string-blt ...)} |
| Pascal | String find | @code{StringFind(haystack, needle)} | @code{(:string-find ...)} |
| Lingo | Bitwise AND | @code{a AND-BIT b} | @code{(:bit-and a b)} |
| Lingo | Bitwise OR | @code{a OR-BIT b} | @code{(:bit-or a b)} |
| Lingo | Bitwise XOR | @code{a XOR-BIT b} | @code{(:bit-xor a b)} |
| Lingo | Bitwise NOT | @code{NOT-BIT a} | @code{(:bit-not a)} |
| Lingo | String length | @code{StringLength(s)} | @code{(:string-length :target s)} |
| Lingo | String substring | @code{StringSubstring(s, start, len)} | @code{(:refmod ...)} |
| Lua | String substring | @code{string.sub(s, start, end)} | @code{(:refmod ...)} |
| Lua | Bit shift | @code{x << n}, @code{x >> n} | @code{(:ash :value x :shift n)} |

All proposed syntax is optional library functions or intuitive operators that extend core language without breaking existing code.

